so I played Final Fantasy 7 remake and  to put it mildly my mind was blown this  is going to be a must play game of 2020  so sit back for 10 minutes and I'll tell  you why oh and definitely download the  chapter 1 demo right now and see for  yourself what all the fuss is about  [Music]  I'm gonna try my best and not talk about  1997 to final fantasy 7 and that lineage  every time I referenced the og game  you'll hear this sound  let's try it Final Fantasy 7 remake for  new players to the series for context  Square Enix invited me down to play  about 4 hours of the remake and here are  my findings  [Music]  I'm starting with three ways to play the  game they feel largely different fights  in Final Fantasy 7 remake are hectic  multiple enemies and allies on screen at  once all beating 10 bells out of each  other  to counteract the hectic combat a touch  of the X button and time almost  standstill  this is a rest buy this is your  opportunity to take stock of events and  decide on your next move  selecting an attack a potion for health  or maybe some magic all of this with a  knowledge that you won't be punished for  taking your time the slowing down of  time is the intended way to play and it  feels great it really does I can't put  into words how it feels so I'll do it in  the noise instead perfect but what if  you don't want time to be affected then  you my friend are a glutton for  punishment but a Final Fantasy 7 remake  has your back by holding down a shoulder  button it is possible to pull off brutal  moves without freezing the fight making  the entire experience go past at  breakneck speeds  so if adrenaline is pumping through your  veins and you don't want the advantage  of bending time use these shortcuts to  play in real time every time the third  way to play is via the classic version  this is designed to play like the  original game but in reality it doesn't  in the og game everything was to  turn-based I honestly thought this was  going to be the way the game played in  classic mode of the remake but hell no  it doesn't instead it does something  very interesting your character will  automatically attack and block for you  it's strange but hear me out I'm not  saying the game will play itself I'm  saying the AI will only be able to keep  you relatively alive and safe and  slightly knock down an opponent's health  bar the onus is still on you to perform  spells heals and alter tax so in essence  the game tries to be playable like a  traditional JRPG and although that isn't  very successful here what it creates  could be a Stressless way to play the  remake so what's your jam AI assists it  completely real time or slow down time  to get the edge  something you won't see in the demo you  can play right now are the summons and  all my word they are impressive back in  1997 we could use summons which gave us  an epic cutscene followed by a single  strike on the enemy well check it out in  the remake we summon gods who once again  have an epic intro but this time they  actually stick around and fight for a  while they can take aggro away from you  they can beat up the boss in front of  your eyes they are in this world for a  small period of time it's essentially  like having another member in your party  and although they aren't here forever  it's longer than I first expected  sadly summons can't be used all the time  they seem to be just here for your time  of need but that could be just the part  that I played so let's not hold our  breath just there let's take a step back  to the narrative Final Fantasy 7 tells  the story of a seemingly terrorist group  attempting to change the world and free  it of huge corporations who harvest the  earth for MACO  let's not go too deep here but that's  the planets lifeforce if that doesn't  interest you in the slightest while this  may not be the game for you because  Final Fantasy 7 remake is completely  story focused and this version is  doubling down on all interactions  between characters the group we are part  of in Chapter 1 will talk to each other  this can happen off screen - this allows  us to see what their character is like  when cloud isn't around and it  surprisingly adds to their personalities  and we start to care if they live or die  all of these are voiced quite  impressively well while impressively  well for a Final Fantasy game but well  are the same the interactions are so  nuanced it's possible to miss things  completely for example not until the  third time I played the demo did I  notice how Barret all pent up with rage  inside an elevator looks over at cloud  and notices how relaxed he is and tries  to lower his own anger by simply  releasing his best subtle storytelling  and character development in video games  we don't see it very often so that's why  I wanted to highlight it there let's  take this point further in Final Fantasy  7 remake flashbacks and hallucinations  will play a huge part of the  storytelling as we uncover clouds  mysterious past expect to jump around in  time regularly  example in Chapter 1 cloud is asked  about Tifa and boom instantly we are  back to their childhood together tea  Verdi going back into combat for a  moment we can switch between characters  I originally thought this would be  superficial they'd all do generally the  same thing with different animations and  I couldn't have been more wrong  each selectable character is a  completely different build cloud is all  about that buster sword and melee at all  opportunities but there are times when  cloud is useless because the enemies are  too far away to jabber sword into that's  where switching to Barret becomes your  play you know them the mr. T crazy fool  guy with the gun for an arm Barret has  ranged attacks and can shoot down an  opposing cannon in seconds later I was  able to play as Tifa just give me a  moment to look at tifa's amazing  personality stiva is a martial arts  expert and like cloud needs to be up  close and personal to get the full  benefit of most of her attacks what's  truly impressive about Tifa is her  ability to combo and link moves together  I found her the hardest to play with but  without a doubt when mastered she will  be unstoppable Aerith on the other hand  is versed in magic and heals the group  to keep them in battle she seems more  defensive than all the rest and her  summons are a sight to be reckoned with  [Music]  from what I've played Final Fantasy 7  remake is a linear game yeah there's a  few little open-world elements to sniff  out and we'll get into sidequest soon  but the story is linear within the story  are decisions to make they won't change  the overarching story beats but  everywhere in the world are ways to  impact gameplay the first opportunity is  when we set the bomb in chapter 1 30  minutes r20 this directly affects how  long you have to escape the facility  later in chapter 2 we'll meet Aerith and  decide on whether we want to buy a  flower or not yeah okay not mind blowing  I get it  but a little variation goes a long way  the most impressive way I saw a  decision-making shape the game was just  before the boss fight with the air  Buster on the way to the battle you'll  discover these key cards which can be  used to weaken the boss  maybe his mobility car is accidentally  defective and thrown in the trash or his  hardest-hitting rockets are disabled  when fighting that big bugger we want  you to fear the robot moving too quickly  or the air barrage will never actually  hit us changing a boss fight before it  even starts brilliant the boss fights  themselves our long and I mean long  between 10 minutes and about half an  hour on average think of boss battles  like those in Monster Hunter or  blood-borne to really understand the  size and scale and longevity of it all  each battle has phases as the boss is  weakened changing tactics on both sides  a farmer each time the battle amped up  the stakes felt greater fighting for 25  minutes to make one false move and ruin  the entire battle is excruciatingly ly  tense oh and just in case you think  you'll be forced to fight the entire 30  minute section again do not worry my  friend auto-saves happen regularly here  including within each boss fight it's  also possible to save when you see fit  no more hunting down a save point like  in 1997 the modern video  game mechanics  [Music]  another important mechanic in Final  Fantasy 7 remake is the stagger system  it's super simple and super rewarding  under each enemy is an orange bar which  slowly fills during a fight max this out  and they will stagger this opens up a  small window of time where two things  happen one they will not be able to  fight back and to any attacks you learn  now will hit harder and hurt them more  so tactically playing to stagger bosses  before hitting them with your limit  breaker is a tip worth telling the  original Final Fantasy 7 was littered  with great minigames like snowboarding  or motorcycle riding we now know that  they are here in the remake so far we've  seen a keep fit competition in a gym and  more subtly in my playthrough a subtle  timing of a switch with other party  members to open a door we'll have to  wait to see if there are more Minds  blowing our mind numbing minigames in  the final version of the game but they  are here and they will break up gameplay  minigames are great oK we've spoken  about combat way too much let's flesh  things out a little  how about side quests although I haven't  played a side quest thus far we know  they exist  thanks to Final Fantasy sevens Twitter  account which highlights some of the  weird and wonderful things we'll be  doing away from the core story mercenary  quests allow us to take bounties from  everyday NPCs such as clearing a factory  of creatures are searching for a friend  in the slums successfully completing  these missions rewards us with items  which could come in handy later on  that's not the end of side quests they  can happen mid story mission - I'm gonna  call them impact quests during the level  in which I fought the air Buster you  know the one where we weakened it by  taking away some of its powers well get  this all those parts that we took away  were available in another room by using  the door timing minigame we looked at we  can venture completely away from the  core story and pick up these items  before they are disposed of allowing us  to use them in the very same battle I  neglected to say this but I got  absolutely punished by the air Buster so  a protip pick up these items it will  make a huge difference in the fight I  think now's a good time to bring this up  Final Fantasy 7 remake is not easy I'm  sure people will be flexing in the  comments below about how easy they think  it'll be but I  say with confidence you will die at some  point in this game even the smallest and  weakest of grunts can surprise cloud in  large-scale battles breaking his attacks  at the worst possible moment after  almost 20 years of games being  surprisingly easy to play Final Fantasy  7 is taking solace in games like Sakura  and Dark Souls and making a game which  will challenge gamers by no means am I  saying this is a Souls born outing but I  am saying Final Fantasy 7 remake will  challenge you constantly  [Music]  in the original game I know I said I  wouldn't talk about original game but I  am now if you played every encounter  correctly cloud would go on a date with  Barrett now that is a real bromance here  in 2020 the dating system is back we  talked about that flower girl Aerith who  gives you a daffodil thing early in the  game well fast forward to the sewer  fight with ABS ooh and that system is in  full flow after falling into the sewers  we must choose who to speak to first  this then makes clouds relationship with  that character stronger and a little bit  more loving who would you choose to  assist first Aerith our Tifa who's your  girl  it's t4 isn't it it's gotta be Tifa it's  Tifa if you said anything else you're  wrong and finally something you may not  notice straight away but it's such a  good implementation it's all about that  soundtrack it's the same soundtrack as  1997 it's been dragged forward into 2020  and lovingly kept the same I mean the  melody is identical what's great here  though is the new dynamic music system  which sees different versions of the  same track switch now effortlessly to  reflect what's happening on the screen  it's always epic but the entire grandeur  of the audio becomes louder more  profound and prouder and more cinematic  depending on your actions the sombre  music of the slums becomes a crescendo  of orchestral brilliance during a fight  in a livingroom environment this will  bring the whole family in to watch you  slay everything in your path and I can  confirm seven days after playing the  game the music is still stuck in my head  and I'm regularly told to keep quiet  so there we have it twenty-one features  in the final fantasy remake how many  times did I reference the first game  [Music]  and by birds I apologize if this looks  like your kind of game please come back  in the future I'll be covering more  Final Fantasy 7 remake in the weeks to  come before its release I'm Adam from  PlayStation granade it's been an  absolute pleasure and I'll see you next  time  [Music]
 

